# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out
coverage.html
coverage/

# Dependency directories
vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# SQLite databases
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/

# Logs
*.log

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/

# sqlc generated code (keep internal/store/sqlite/*.go)
# We commit sqlc generated code to avoid requiring sqlc for builds

# Chronos specific
chronos.db
.chronos/

# Claude Code per-clone permissions and runtime state. Project-level
# .claude/ may host shared agents in future, but settings.local.json
# is by design local-only (the file name carries the intent).
.claude/

# coverctl profile output (regenerated each run); .coverctl.yaml is tracked
.cover/

# nox transient outputs (sarif/cdx/findings produced per run);
# .nox/baseline.json IS tracked so CI gates on new findings only.
.nox/out/
.nox/cache/

# Default-output-dir landing pad: when nox scan is invoked without
# -output, findings.json drops at cwd and would re-pollute itself
# on the next scan.
/findings.json
/results.sarif
/sbom.cdx.json
/sbom.spdx.json
/report.html

# Roady journal files. spec.yaml / spec.lock.json / policy.yaml /
# plan.json / state.json carry the durable shape and stay tracked;
# events.jsonl (append-only transition log) and usage.json
# (per-actor usage metrics) are per-clone bookkeeping. Keeping them
# out of version control also drops ~1100 spurious nox findings
# (UUIDs in the journal trip secret-detection heuristics).
.roady/events.jsonl
.roady/usage.json

# Relicta release tooling
.relicta/
ai.inventory.json

# The `chronos` binary at the repo root is a build artefact: `make docker-build`
# stages it with `cp $(BUILD_DIR)/$(BINARY_NAME) chronos` and removes it again
# with `rm -f chronos`. Committing it between those two steps put a 30 MB
# unattested Mach-O executable in every clone, on a repo whose shipped image is
# Linux. Ignore the path so it cannot come back.
/chronos
